A||||6||DaRkLoRD||Smokey Yunick  1924-2001||||9||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||07-06-2001||01:19 PM||||One of the greatest people in the automotive industry is gone.. There was a brief writeup about Smokey in this month's Hot Rod magazine, including a photo of him standing with his Fiero.. The writeup mentions a book about him, I think I'll look into getting it, if it has any info about his hot vapor engine system. It's really a shame that he died before anyone started using vapor fuel engines... the tech is out there, and has the capacity to drastically improve the efficiency of our cars, while maintaining performance. I have some scanned articles somewhere from 1984-85 about the mods Smokey did to an 84 Fiero. I'll try and find them..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||ChadMan||07-06-2001||01:35 PM||||Smokey was cool.  In addition to his engine wizardry, didn't he also come up with some (ahem) creative NASCAR stuff in the '60s, like a Fairlane with a drooping nose and high tail for aerodynamics and a complete Chevelle built to 7/8 scale?||||reg||9
