Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||07-06-2001||09:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by horseman:<BR><B>Smokey Yunick achieved 250HP out of the duke while getting  50+MPG. The only internal mod was a camshaft change. The key was in the exhaust and induction setups. Don't take my word for it;goto Hot Rod archives and get the June'84 article titled "Smokey's New Hot Air Engine...THE NEXT STEP <BR>If I ever find the time, I will have a similar engine in my fiero. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>He also used an experimental vapor fuel system, and if he'd kept the car at stock HP levels he could have had MUCH higher mileage... as many of my forum friends might be aware of, after listening to me talk about this until very early in the morning on the chat.....<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
